  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or confirmed the rule runs without errors.\n\n**Data:** The data view has a `timestamp` field, `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`), `extension`, `bytes`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `url`, `request`, `host` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-5f84b95f Web logs overview\" has four panels and defaults to the last 7 days. Its ID is `eff-5f84b95f-web-logs-overview-90e40e5b002e`, and it opens at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-5f84b95f-web-logs-overview-90e40e5b002e. The panels are:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Average bytes by file extension\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-5f84b95f 5xx spike\" (ID `53e9dc1b-15f7-418f-9e41-fb59347175be`) is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 documents match a 5-minute window. The match is a prefix query for `5` on `response.keyword`, which catches every 5xx code. It was created disabled, and I then enabled it.\n\nThe rule has no action connector attached, so it will show alerts in Kibana but won't send a notification anywhere.",
